This product is a from-scratch Kotlin Multiplatform implementation of
established audio container and coding formats.

Everything in this release was written from published specifications, not
translated from another implementation:

  RIFF WAVE and WAVE_FORMAT_EXTENSIBLE   Microsoft multimedia programming
                                         documentation
  RF64 and BW64                          EBU Tech 3306, EBU Tech 3285
  Wave64                                 Sony Wave64 specification
  AIFF and AIFF-C                        Apple Audio Interchange File Format
                                         1.3 and AIFF-C
  AU                                     Sun and NeXT audio file format
                                         documentation
  A-law and mu-law                       ITU-T Recommendation G.711
  IMA and DVI ADPCM                      IMA Digital Audio Focus and Technical
                                         Working Group recommended practices,
                                         and Microsoft's IMA ADPCM WAVE type
                                         documentation
  Microsoft ADPCM                        Microsoft ADPCM WAVE type
                                         documentation
  QuickTime IMA (ima4)                   Apple QuickTime File Format
                                         documentation

Formats named by the sniffer but not decoded are identified from their
published magic numbers only.

Test oracles are used as external programs and never read or redistributed as
source. The suites that compare against ffmpeg skip themselves when it is not
installed.

reference/REFERENCES.md records every specification consulted, and, for the
work still to come, which permissively licensed implementations may be ported
from. GPL and LGPL sources are out of bounds for this project and are listed
there so the boundary stays explicit.

Deliberate exclusions, so that a reader knows they are decisions rather than
gaps waiting to be filled:

  WMA has no open specification and no permissively licensed implementation.
  TAK and OptimFROG are closed source.
  Shorten has a restrictive licence history and no current use.
  DTS and Enhanced AC-3 are named by the sniffer and will not be decoded while
  their patent positions remain unclear.
